<ltml units="in" margin="0.55">
  <layout id="vbox" vpadding="15pt" />
  <font id="contrast" size="18" color="Black" weight="Bold" />
  <brush id="linear-gradient" kind="linear-gradient" units="in" x0="0" y0="0" x1="6.4" y1="1.1" stops="0:#1d4ed8,0.5:#0f766e,1:#f59e0b" />
  <brush id="radial-gradient" kind="radial-gradient" units="in" x0="1.45" y0="0.45" r0="0" x1="1.45" y1="0.45" r1="0.95" stops="0:#fff7ed,0.55:#fdba74,1:#c2410c" />
  <brush id="metal" kind="image" src="../../docs/assets/metal-movable-type-banner.jpg" opacity="0.5" />

  <page layout="vbox">
    <label font.size="19" font.weight="Bold">Widget background brushes</label>
    <p>Gradient and image background fills are routed through shared widget background painting.</p>

    <vbox width="100%" border="thin" padding="10pt" corners="0.25" fill="linear-gradient">
      <label font.size="15" font.weight="Bold" font.color="White">Container gradient background</label>
      <p font.color="WhiteSmoke">A plain div uses the same shared widget background brush path as labels and paragraphs.</p>
    </vbox>

    <table cols="2" order="rows">
      <label padding="10pt" border="thin" fill="radial-gradient">
        Label with radial brush background
      </label>
      <p padding="10pt" border="thin" font="contrast" fill="metal"
        fill.fit="cover"
        fill.anchor="center">
        Paragraph background images now flow through the same shared widget background painter, with the image drawn into a clipped widget box.
      </p>
    </table>

    <vbox border="thin" padding="10pt" corners="0.25" font="contrast" fill="metal"
      fill.fit="tile"
      fill.tile-height="100%"
      fill.repeat="repeat-x"
      fill.anchor="top-left">
      <label font.weight="Bold">Tiled image background</label>
      <p>This panel uses a full-height tile plus horizontal repeat so high-resolution artwork still fills the box vertically while demonstrating visible tiling.</p>
    </vbox>
  </page>
</ltml>
